   'A SHOE CHART IS A TRANSLATOR, NOT AN ESTIMATOR — the size CANNOT be measured from a photo. It is STAMPED on the tongue label or the insole and must be READ, then converted; the foot-length inches are a sanity check for a shoe in hand. FILA SELLS SHOES AND CLOTHES UNDER ONE NAME, so settle the GARMENT TYPE before reading the size: a stamped 9 on this chart is a shoe, an M on the Fila tops chart is a chest. Never carry one onto the other. FILA-SPECIFIC: roughly true to size, though the DISRUPTOR runs a touch LARGE and is often sized down a half — state the stamped number so the buyer can judge. Condition note for the Disruptor: the white midsole YELLOWS progressively and irreversibly, and that is a real value lever; its oversized sole is DESIGNED and is not deformity. Standard US/UK/EU grade and the reported resale consensus, not Fila-published specs — capped confidence.',
   'https://www.fila.com/', 0.50, false, 'migration:00465'),
